Chapter One - The Ancestors of Jesus Christ
These are the names of Jesus Christ's ancestors, son of David, son of Abraham:
Ibrahim was Isaac's son, and Isaac was Jacob's son, and Jacob was Judah and his brothers' son.
Judah fathered Perez and Zerah by Tamar. Perez fathered Hezron, and Hezron fathered Aram.
Aram was the father of Amminadab, who was the father of Nahshon, who was the father of Salmon.
Salmon was the son of Boaz from Rahab, Boaz was the son of Obed from Ruth, and Obed was the son of Jesse.
ويسي هو ابن داوود الملك. وداوود ابنه سليمان من الست اللي كان متجوزها اوريا.
Solomon was Rehoboam's son, Rehoboam was Abijah's son, and Abijah was Asa's son.
Asaph was the son of Jehoshaphat, who was the son of Joram, who was the son of Uzziah.
Uzziah was the son of Jotham, Jotham was the son of Ahaz, and Ahaz was the son of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the son of Manasseh, who was the son of Amos, who was the son of Josiah.
Josiah was the son of Jehoiachin and his brothers during the time when the Jews were exiled in Babylon.
And after they returned from Babylon, Jeconiah fathered Shealtiel, and Shealtiel fathered Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the son of Shealtiel, who was the son of Neri, who was the son of Malchi.
Azor was the son of Sadoc, who was the son of Ahimaaz, who was the son of Eliud.
And Eliud was the father of Eleazar, and Eleazar the father of Matthan, and Matthan the father of Jacob.
Jacob was Joseph's father, who was Mary's husband, who gave birth to Jesus, who is called Christ.
All generations from Abraham to David were fourteen generations; and from David until the deportation to Babylon were fourteen generations; and from the deportation to Babylon until the birth of Christ were fourteen generations. The birth of Jesus Christ
This is how Jesus Christ was born: Mary was engaged to Joseph but before they were married, she became pregnant through the power of the Holy Spirit. Luke
Youssef's fiancé was a good man who didn't want to shame her, so he decided to divorce her secretly.
While he was thinking about this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream and said, "Joseph son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary home as your wife, because what is conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
She will give birth to a son, and you are to give him the name Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins." - Luke
And all this happened so that God's word would be fulfilled through the prophet who said:
"The farm will give birth to a boy who will be named Emmanuel," which means "God is with us."
When Yusuf was tired from sleepiness, he did what the angel of God had commanded him to do and married Maryam.
But he did not have sexual relations with her until she gave birth to a son; and he named him Jesus. Luke 2:21
The second chapter - The wise men came to see Jesus
When Jesus was born in Bethlehem in Judea, during King Herod's reign, some wise men came from the east to Jerusalem, guided by a star
Kaysolo: "Where is this king of Jews who was born? We saw his star in the east and have come to worship him."
When King Herod heard this, he was terrified, and so were all the people in Jerusalem.
He gathered together all the heads of religion and law scholars and asked them: "Where was Christ born?"
They answered him: "The house of flesh is in Judea where this thing was written about by the prophet when he said:"
And you Bethlehem, in the land of Judah, from you will come forth a ruler who will shepherd my people Israel."
After Herod sent for the wise men to find out from them when the star had appeared, he questioned them carefully about this.
And after sending them to Bethlehem, he said to them, "Go back home now. When you find him, come tell me so I can go worship him too."
When they heard what the king said, they left. And there appeared to them the star that they had seen when it rose, and it went forward before them until it came to rest over the place where the child was.
And when they saw the star, they were overjoyed.
When they entered the house, they saw the child with Mary his mother. They bowed down and worshipped him. Then they opened their treasure chests and presented him with gold and frankincense and myrrh.
And so God sent them an angel in a dream telling them to go back home without going near Herod. They took another road and went back to their country. Jesus' family fled to Egypt
After the wise men left, an angel appeared to Joseph in a dream and said: "Get up, take the child and his mother and flee to Egypt, stay there until I tell you when it's safe to return, because Herod is going to search for the child to kill him."
Joseph got up, took his son, and left at night to go down to Egypt.
And it came to pass that Herod killed all the children in Bethlehem who were two years old and under, according to what was spoken by the prophet Jeremiah: "A voice is heard in Ramah, weeping and much lamentation; Rachel weeping for her children"
When Herod saw that he had been tricked by these wise men, he was furious and ordered all the children in Bethlehem and its surrounding areas from two years old and under to be killed, because this is how much time had passed since they told him about it.
And so it was fulfilled what the Lord had said through the prophet Jeremiah:
From Rama you hear wailing, weeping and loud lamentation; Rachel is weeping for her children and she refuses to be comforted because they are dead. Jesus' family returns from Egypt
When Herod died, an angel of the Lord appeared to Joseph in Egypt in a dream
He said to him: "Get up, take the boy and go back to Israel, because those who wanted to kill the boy have died."
Joseph got up, took his son, and returned to Israel.
But when he heard that Archelaus was ruling in Judea instead of his father Herod, he was afraid to go back there. And because an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream, he went to live in Galilee.
He came to a city called Nazareth and lived there, so that what was said through the prophets might be fulfilled: "He will be called a Nazarene." Mark 1:24; Luke 2:39; John 1:45
