Jesus wept over his disciples and said to them: "Stay with these people for three days; they have been with me without food." And I don't want to send them away hungry so that they won't faint along the way."
And they said to him: "Where can we get enough bread in this place to feed such a crowd?"
Jesus asked them, "How many loaves do you have?" They replied, "Seven loaves and a few small fish."
And Jesus ordered the crowd to sit down on the ground.
And he took those seven loaves and fish, gave thanks to God, broke them up, and gave them to his disciples; and they in turn served them to the crowds.
They all ate until they were full, and then they left with seven bags filled with bread crumbs that had fallen from their mouths.
They were 2500 people without women and children.
And he sent his disciples in a boat across to the other side of the lake while he dismissed the crowds.
Chapter 14 Signs of the Times
Some Pharisees and Sadducees came to Jesus to test him. They asked him to show them a sign from heaven. Matthew
But he answered them, "When it is evening you say, 'It will be fair weather, for the sky is red.'
In the early morning he said to them: "Today it will be cold, because the sky is red and overcast." You know how to interpret weather conditions, but you can't explain the signs of time!
An evil and corrupt generation asks for a sign; but no sign will be given it except the sign of Jonah.” And he left them and went away. Matthew 12:39; Luke 11:29 The yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees
When they reached the other side of the sea, they forgot to take bread with them.
Jesus said to them, "Watch out and beware of the yeast of the Pharisees and Sadducees." - Luke
They said to themselves: "He's telling us this because we didn't bring bread with us."
Jesus knew what they were thinking and said to them, "Why do you have such little faith? Are you still so blind that you don't see?"
Haven't you understood yet? Haven't you realized that five loaves were distributed to five thousand people, and how many baskets full did they collect from the leftover bread?
And you didn't count how many loaves were distributed to four thousand people and how much money was collected?
How could you fail to understand that I was talking about bread when I said this? You have your minds all closed up by the teachings of the Pharisees and Sadducees!”
And you're right, he told them to stay away from teaching the Pharisees and Sadducees, and also from yeast in bread. Peter testifies that Jesus is the Christ
When Jesus came to Caesarea Philippi, he asked his disciples, "Who do people say that I am?"
And they said to him, "Some say John the Baptist, others Elijah, and still others Jeremiah or one of the prophets." Matthew
And he said to them: "Who am I that you should be afraid of me?"
Simon Peter answered, "You are the Christ, the Son of the living God!" - John
Jesus said to him, "Simon son of Jonah, you are blessed because this was not revealed to you by flesh and blood, but by my Father in heaven."
And I tell you this: You are Peter, and upon this rock I will build my church, and the gates of hell shall not prevail against it.
"And I will give you the keys to the kingdom of heaven; whatever you bind on earth shall be bound in heaven, and whatever you loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven."
After Jesus told his disciples to keep quiet about who he was, he prophesied about his death and resurrection.
From that time Jesus began to show his disciples that he must go to Jerusalem and suffer many things from the elders and chief priests and scribes, and be killed, and on the third day be raised.
Peter pulled him to one side and started arguing with him saying: "No way sir! This can't be happening!"
And he turned to Peter and said, "Get behind me, Satan! You're an obstacle to me because you don't have in mind God's concerns but man's."
And Jesus said to his disciples: "If anyone wants to come after me, let him deny himself and take up his cross daily and follow me."
He who wants to save his life will lose it, but he who loses his life for my sake will find it. When?
What good is it for someone to gain the whole world but forfeit their own life? Or what can they give in exchange for their life?
When will the Son of Man come with his angels in all his glory? Then he will reward each person according to what they have done.
And I tell you the truth: there is someone here who will not die until he sees the Son of Man coming in his kingdom.”
Chapter 17 Jesus appeared in his glory
After six days, Jesus took Peter and James and John his brother up a high mountain by themselves.
He changed his shape before their eyes; he was like the sun in splendor, and his clothes were white as light.
And they saw Moses and Elijah talking with Jesus.
Peter said to Jesus, "How good it is for us to be here! If you wish, I will put up three shelters—one for you, one for Moses, and one for Elijah."
And while he was speaking, a bright cloud overshadowed them; and a voice came from the cloud, saying, "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased; listen to him!" 2 Peter 1:17-18
When they heard this, they fell to their faces in fear.
Jesus came up to them in the boat, reached out his hand, took hold of them and said to them, "Take heart, it is I; do not be afraid!"
They rolled their eyes and saw that Jesus was alone.
As they were going down from the mountain, Jesus commanded them, "Don't tell anyone what you have seen until after the Son of Man has risen from the dead."
They asked him: "Why do scholars say that Elijah must come first?"
He answered them by saying: "In fact, Elijah Gheiji is the one who will come and fix everything."
But I tell you that Elijah has already come, and they didn't recognize him; they did to him everything they wanted, just as it will be with the Son of Man also." - Matthew 17:12-13
And he said to them, "Go tell John what you have seen and heard: the blind receive their sight, the lame walk, lepers are cleansed, and the deaf hear, the dead are raised up, the poor have good news preached to them." And blessed is he who takes no offense at me.
When Jesus and his disciples arrived at the crowd, a man came to him and knelt down before him.
He said: "Have mercy on my son, sir! He's suffering so much, he gets beaten up often, and many times he falls down in pain."
"He was your student, but they couldn't save him."
Jesus answered, "How long shall I stay with you? How long must I put up with you?" Then he called for the boy.
Jesus got up and ordered the demon to leave the boy, and it did so at that moment.
The disciples came to Jesus and asked him privately, "Why couldn't we drive it out?"
He said to them, "Because of your little faith! I tell you the truth, if you have faith as small as a mustard seed, you can say to this mountain, 'Move from here to there,' and it will move. Nothing will be impossible for you."
And this type of madness can only be cured through prayer and fasting." This verse is absent from many ancient manuscripts Matthew 21:21; Mark 11:23; 1 Corinthians 13:2 Jesus prophesies again about his death and resurrection
And his disciples were gathered together in Galilee; and he said unto them, The Son of man shall be delivered up into the hands of men.
They killed him, but on the third day he will rise again." The disciples were deeply saddened. Jesus paid the temple tax
When Jesus returned to Capernaum with his disciples, some tax collectors from the temple approached Peter and asked him: "Doesn't your teacher pay the temple tax?"
He answered them, "Yes, he will pay." When Peter went inside the house, Jesus asked him, "What do you think Simon? From whom do earthly kings collect taxes or fees? From their own children or from others?"
Peter answered him, "From outsiders." Then Jesus said to him, "Are their children exempt from paying taxes?"
But don't cause them any trouble, go to the sea and cast your line, and the first fish that bites, cut its mouth open, and you will find four coins in it. Take them and get yourself something to eat."
